{
  "_README": [
    "Frozen board hashes. Generated by scripts/check-determinism.mjs --update from",
    "clean code; asserted by `npm run check:determinism` and by CI on every push.",
    "",
    "A failure here means a code change re-rolled a board that players have already",
    "seen: past dailies would regenerate differently and every shared challenge link",
    "would break. That is almost never what you want — if it IS intended, it is a new",
    "scoring era and needs a version gate (see CLAUDE.md), not an updated hash.",
    "",
    "Per board, two hashes (see scripts/lib/board.mjs):",
    "  pop  — sha256(populationMap). The hash the CLAUDE.md protocol documents;",
    "         the 2026-07-08 values below match its recorded constants exactly.",
    "  full — sha256({pop, counties}). Counties draw from the same rng stream but",
    "         AFTER the population map, so only this catches countyGenerator drift.",
    "",
    "Anchors span both tiers, both assigned parties (party sets bluePercentage, so",
    "blue and red days generate genuinely different boards) and several seeds.",
    "",
    "`model` pins which board-model ERA a date belongs to (1 = pre-Beta, 2 = Beta,",
    "the boundary being MODEL_V2_UTC in rng.js). It is asserted, not decorative:",
    "moving that constant re-rolls every date that changes side just as surely as",
    "editing the generator, and this makes the check name that cause directly.",
    "BOTH eras must stay green forever — v1 is what the archive and every old",
    "challenge link replay, v2 is every board from 2026-07-20 on.",
    "",
    "2026-07-19 and 2026-07-20 are deliberately adjacent: they are the last v1 day",
    "and the first v2 day, so they fence the era boundary from both sides.",
    "",
    "NOTE: the era boundary is 2026-07-20 (MODEL_V2_UTC). It is NOT the 'Beta",
    "launch' date the landing page counts down to (2026-08-01) — that one is",
    "promotional and lives in hooks/useBetaCountdown.js. Do not reconcile them."
  ],
